<.dm_breadcrumb class="px-4">
  <:crumb to={~p"/components/navigation/left-menu"}>Navigation</:crumb>
  <:crumb>Left Menu</:crumb>
</.dm_breadcrumb>

<.dm_card class="w-full h-full overflow-auto" body_class="p-4">
  <:title class="flex flex-row justify-center items-center gap-3">
    <span class="text-4xl text-primary">Left Menu</span>
    <span class="text-sm opacity-60">dm_left_menu, dm_left_menu_group</span>
  </:title>

  <.dm_markdown content={"""
  ## Overview
  Sidebar navigation menu with native groups and an optional collapsible icon rail.

  ## Usage
  ```elixir
  <.dm_left_menu active="dashboard">
    <:title>Navigation</:title>
    <:menu>
      <.dm_left_menu_group active="dashboard">
        <:title>Main</:title>
        <:menu id="dashboard" to="/dashboard">Dashboard</:menu>
        <:menu id="settings" to="/settings">Settings</:menu>
      </.dm_left_menu_group>
    </:menu>
  </.dm_left_menu>
  ```
  """} />

  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4">Collapsible Sidebar</h3>
  <p class="mb-4">
    The live example has 24 pages, a sticky sidebar and a bottom collapse button.
    Scroll the menu, close a group, then navigate or use Back and Forward to check
    that its state survives. Hover or focus a collapsed link to see its label.
  </p>
  <.link href={~p"/components/navigation/left-menu/live/dashboard"} class="btn btn-primary mb-6">
    Open persistent sidebar example
  </.link>
  <.link
    href={~p"/components/navigation/left-menu/live/dashboard?controlled=true"}
    class="btn btn-outline mb-6"
  >
    Open host-owned state example
  </.link>

  <.dm_markdown content={"""
  ## Sticky layout and page navigation

  Register all package hooks using `import * as DuskmoonHooks from "phoenix_duskmoon/hooks"`
  in your LiveSocket options. The component attaches `DuskmoonLeftMenu` and
  `DuskmoonLeftMenuNavigation` automatically.

  In the shared **LiveView layout**, pass menu data and the current page directly:

  ```heex
  <.dm_left_menu
    id="admin-sidebar"
    sticky
    socket={@socket}
    groups={@menu_groups}
    active={@active_nav}
    brand={%{label: "Administration", icon: "view-dashboard"}}
    footer_text="My application"
    storage_key="my-app:admin-sidebar-collapsed"
    class="sticky top-0 h-dvh"
  />
  ```

  Each group is a map with string `id`, `label`, optional `open` and `items`.
  Each item needs string `id`, `label`, `to`, and optionally an MDI `icon`,
  `disabled`, `class` and `rest`. Use atom keys, unique IDs, and server-filtered
  menu data. Sticky mode accepts data instead of slots and enables the icon rail.
  Existing slot-based menus remain available without `sticky`.

  CSS `class="sticky top-0 h-dvh"` positions the menu and bounds its height;
  `sticky socket={@socket}` keeps its package-owned child alive across LiveView
  pages. The brand, footer and toggle stay fixed while only the menu body scrolls.
  CSS sticky remains constrained by its containing block and scrolling ancestors.
  For a top app bar, adjust both the offset and available height.

  The component owns collapse, group state, navigation scroll restoration and
  active-item synchronization. Supply the same menu ID and configuration on every
  destination page; changing only `active` preserves the child. Pass an empty
  string to clear highlighting. Changing groups, brand or presentation settings
  changes the configuration hash and remounts the child with current menu data.
  No application sidebar LiveView, navigation hook or event handler is required.

  For host session persistence, opt into `collapse_controlled`, pass authoritative
  `collapsed`, omit `storage_key`, and set `collapse_event` to a custom event name.
  User toggles emit a bubbling CustomEvent with `detail: {id, collapsed}`. The host
  validates and persists that boolean. Changed controlled values preserve the
  sticky child. A targeted `duskmoon:left-menu:set-collapsed` DOM event applies
  `detail: {collapsed: true}` silently, without notification or storage writes.
  The host-owned example uses parent LiveView assigns and server controls; a real
  session store belongs to the host application.

  Full HTTP navigation or a reload resets in-memory scroll and group state.
  Optional `storage_key` persists only the collapsed preference. See the
  [left-menu guide](https://hexdocs.pm/phoenix_duskmoon/left-menu.html)
  for the data format, shared layout and browser verification steps.

  """} />

  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4">Menu with Groups</h3>
  <div class="w-64 bg-base-200 rounded-lg">
    <.dm_left_menu active="item-1">
      <:title class="font-bold text-primary">Demo Menu</:title>
      <:menu>
        <.dm_left_menu_group active="item-1">
          <:title>Section A</:title>
          <:menu id="item-1" to="#">
            <.dm_mdi name="home" class="w-4 h-4" /> Dashboard
          </:menu>
          <:menu id="item-2" to="#">
            <.dm_mdi name="account" class="w-4 h-4" /> Profile
          </:menu>
        </.dm_left_menu_group>
      </:menu>
      <:menu>
        <.dm_left_menu_group active="item-1">
          <:title>Section B</:title>
          <:menu id="item-3" to="#">
            <.dm_mdi name="cog" class="w-4 h-4" /> Settings
          </:menu>
          <:menu id="item-4" to="#" disabled={true}>
            <.dm_mdi name="lock" class="w-4 h-4" /> Locked
          </:menu>
        </.dm_left_menu_group>
      </:menu>
    </.dm_left_menu>
  </div>

  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4">Menu Link Tooltips</h3>
  <p class="mb-4">
    Spread tooltip trigger attributes onto a menu slot to attach hover and keyboard-focus hints
    to its navigation link. Use the slot's <code>rest</code> map for other global link attributes.
  </p>
  <div class="w-64 bg-base-200 rounded-lg">
    <.dm_tooltip
      :let={trigger_attrs}
      id="left-menu-dashboard-hint"
      content="Dashboard"
      position="right"
    >
      <.dm_left_menu_group active="dashboard">
        <:title>Workspace</:title>
        <:menu
          id="dashboard"
          to={~p"/components/navigation/left-menu"}
          rest={%{"aria-label" => "Dashboard"}}
          {trigger_attrs}
        >
          <.dm_mdi name="view-dashboard" class="w-4 h-4" aria-hidden="true" />
        </:menu>
      </.dm_left_menu_group>
    </.dm_tooltip>
  </div>

  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-4">Sizes</h3>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
    <div class="w-48 bg-base-200 rounded-lg">
      <.dm_left_menu size="xs">
        <:title>XS Menu</:title>
        <:menu>
          <.dm_left_menu_group>
            <:title>Items</:title>
            <:menu id="xs-1" to="#">Item 1</:menu>
            <:menu id="xs-2" to="#">Item 2</:menu>
          </.dm_left_menu_group>
        </:menu>
      </.dm_left_menu>
    </div>
    <div class="w-64 bg-base-200 rounded-lg">
      <.dm_left_menu size="lg">
        <:title>LG Menu</:title>
        <:menu>
          <.dm_left_menu_group>
            <:title>Items</:title>
            <:menu id="lg-1" to="#">Item 1</:menu>
            <:menu id="lg-2" to="#">Item 2</:menu>
          </.dm_left_menu_group>
        </:menu>
      </.dm_left_menu>
    </div>
  </div>
</.dm_card>
